  "details": "Since the latest update, when I turn my head in VR, there is a visible jitter/stutter that happens in the viewport. This happens in every world I'm in, even the default VRC home (which I assume is very optimized). \n\nFor reference, I am on Quest 3 Virtual Desktop PCVR. I checked for visual stuttering in SteamVR home, and in the Meta home. Both work fine. The stuttering only happens when I'm in a world in VRC (does not happen on loading screen). \n\nI have no idea what's going on; I changed nothing, and it worked perfectly fine last week, prior to the latest update. It's frustrating, because it's giving me a headache.",
